---
title: Localized Defaults
description: Select default resources by language and output one or several configuration files.
---

## Resource layout

```text
src/main/resources/defaults/lang/en.yml
src/main/resources/defaults/lang/ja.yml
src/main/resources/defaults/lang/ja_JP.yml
```

Use a resource directory with `fromResource(...)`. `pull(file)` resolves the language at load time and chooses the output file. Existing output files are retained; selecting a language does not translate an existing file.

## One output file

```kotlin
import net.ririfa.yacla.Yacla
import net.ririfa.yacla.yaml.YamlParser
import java.nio.file.Paths

val loader = Yacla.loader<AppConfig>()
    .fromResource("/defaults/lang/")
    .parser(YamlParser())
    .language("ja_JP")
    .defaultLanguage("en")
    .pull(Paths.get("config.yml"))
    .load()
```

Without `.language(...)`, the JVM locale is used. The default fallback is `en`. For `ja_JP`, resolution tries `ja_JP` then `ja`, followed by fallback-language candidates. Both `ja-JP` and `ja_JP` inputs are accepted; hyphens are normalized to underscores.

For YAML, each candidate tries `yml` then `yaml`. JSON uses `json`. If no selected or fallback resource exists, loading fails with the tried paths.

`pull("ja", file)` combines explicit language selection and output configuration. `systemLanguage()` resets selection to the JVM locale.

## Multiple files

```kotlin
import net.ririfa.yacla.LanguageOutputMode

val loader = Yacla.loader<AppConfig>()
    .fromResource("/defaults/lang/")
    .parser(YamlParser())
    .language("ja")
    .defaultLanguage("en")
    .languageOutputMode(LanguageOutputMode.MULTIPLE_FILES)
    .outputLanguages("en", "ja")
    .pull(Paths.get("config.yml"))
    .load()
```

This writes missing `config_en.yml` and `config_ja.yml` and loads the selected Japanese file. Resolution includes requested output languages, the selected language, and the fallback language. Missing languages resolve to the fallback resource; duplicate resolved outputs are removed. Suffixes use the resolved resource's language.

Automatic and manual updates apply to the active selected file. The other output files are initially copied if missing, but are not all updated by the active loader.
